  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Medline Industries has $91.6M in federal contract obligations in FY2027 to date. Medline Industries received 119 awards this fiscal year so far, with an average award size of $770K. Obligations fell 90.7% year over year. Historical obligations show a peak in FY26 at $987M, and earlier totals of $579M in FY25, $370M in FY24, $337M in FY23, and $281M in FY22. The Department of Veterans Affairs is the primary buyer, accounting for $89.1M of FY2027 obligations. The Department of Justice and the Department of Health and Human Services follow with $2.2M and $257K respectively. Medline Industries’ FY2027 obligations are concentrated in the Medical, Dental, and Hospital Equipment and Supplies Merchant Wholesalers market at $91.1M, with smaller amounts in Surgical and Medical Instrument Manufacturing at $573K and General Medical and Surgical Hospitals at $10K. This profile shows FY2027 obligations clustered with one agency and one market to date.",
